WEBVTT

1
00:00:06.000 --> 00:00:12.074
Do you want subtitles for any video?
-=[ ai.OpenSubtitles.com ]=-

2
00:00:37.087 --> 00:00:38.087
Clay.

3
00:00:39.213 --> 00:00:40.503
Clay. help me!

4
00:00:41.382 --> 00:00:42.462
He was hurt.

5
00:00:43.342 --> 00:00:44.342
Dying.

6
00:00:48.137 --> 00:00:49.553
And I couldn't help him.

7
00:00:55.352 --> 00:00:57.394
I just watched him bleed.

8
00:00:59.439 --> 00:01:01.523
Jesus. Clay. Come on. Help me.

9
00:01:01.525 --> 00:01:02.815
Uh...

10
00:01:05.569 --> 00:01:06.610
Clay!

11
00:01:08.864 --> 00:01:11.489
Clay! Clay. what the fuck?

12
00:01:11.491 --> 00:01:13.411
And... time!

13
00:01:17.413 --> 00:01:19.583
I'm afraid your victim
didn't make it. guys.

14
00:01:22.876 --> 00:01:25.835
- Sorry.
- Let's see how other teams did.

15
00:01:27.088 --> 00:01:29.239
Wow. You guys really nailed it. huh?

16
00:01:29.241 --> 00:01:31.468
Really nice work on the bandages too.

17
00:01:32.427 --> 00:01:35.301
I just figured close range
with a clean exit point.

18
00:01:35.303 --> 00:01:38.096
Probably best to apply constant
pressure with a compress.

19
00:01:38.098 --> 00:01:39.639
It would really be more realistic

20
00:01:39.641 --> 00:01:43.225
for us to deal with a high-velocity.
high-impact wound.

21
00:01:43.227 --> 00:01:44.977
like a .223 from an assault rifle.

22
00:01:46.022 --> 00:01:47.852
Those are illegal in California. no?

23
00:01:48.648 --> 00:01:50.028
No. yeah. they are.

24
00:01:53.236 --> 00:01:55.737
Hey. great work. everyone.

25
00:01:55.739 --> 00:01:59.612
Look. I know this can
be a tough exercise.

26
00:01:59.614 --> 00:02:01.867
but it only takes two to five minutes

27
00:02:01.869 --> 00:02:05.578
for someone to bleed out
from a gunshot wound. Right?

28
00:02:05.580 --> 00:02:06.871
Our goal today is to...

29
00:02:06.873 --> 00:02:09.832
A tourniquet would do
fuck-all when a single bullet

30
00:02:09.834 --> 00:02:11.916
from an AR-15 rips open your insides.

31
00:02:11.918 --> 00:02:13.376
So. how about this?

32
00:02:13.378 --> 00:02:15.045
Instead of teaching
us to stop the bleed.

33
00:02:15.047 --> 00:02:17.505
they make it less likely
we'll actually get shot

34
00:02:17.507 --> 00:02:21.383
at our own fucking high school?
Wouldn't that make more sense?

35
00:02:21.385 --> 00:02:24.305
It must be upsetting to go
through that kind of training.

36
00:02:25.139 --> 00:02:26.889
This is when I lose respect for you.

37
00:02:26.891 --> 00:02:29.098
when you ask the most obvious question.

38
00:02:29.934 --> 00:02:32.212
Would you rather I presume

39
00:02:32.214 --> 00:02:34.562
to know how you feel without asking?

40
00:02:34.564 --> 00:02:36.688
Okay. now you're just arguing.

41
00:02:36.690 --> 00:02:38.030
I don't mean to be.

42
00:02:40.110 --> 00:02:42.860
How'd the stop-the-bleed
exercise make you feel?

43
00:02:45.323 --> 00:02:46.323
Helpless.

44
00:02:48.910 --> 00:02:51.785
It's awful. Feeling helpless
is the worst feeling there is.

45
00:02:51.787 --> 00:02:54.579
- Tell me why.
- I mean. isn't that obvious?

46
00:02:54.581 --> 00:02:56.581
Let's say it's not.

47
00:02:56.583 --> 00:03:00.459
Why is feeling helpless. for you.
the worst feeling there is?

48
00:03:00.461 --> 00:03:02.541
Is helping people important to you?

49
00:03:05.382 --> 00:03:06.881
Isn't that important to you?

50
00:03:06.883 --> 00:03:09.633
Very. and sometimes I can't help them.

51
00:03:12.222 --> 00:03:14.141
And what do you do?

52
00:03:15.808 --> 00:03:17.478
Well. I try...

53
00:03:18.560 --> 00:03:20.520
everything I know to try.

54
00:03:22.814 --> 00:03:24.604
I consult with colleagues.

55
00:03:26.734 --> 00:03:27.944
but in the end.

56
00:03:30.237 --> 00:03:32.278
if I can't help a patient.

57
00:03:32.280 --> 00:03:34.280
then I try to find someone who can.

58
00:03:41.247 --> 00:03:42.577
But after all that.

59
00:03:43.791 --> 00:03:45.998
are certain people beyond help?

60
00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.708
I hope not.

61
00:03:47.710 --> 00:03:49.630
Do you worry that you're beyond help?

62
00:03:51.387 --> 00:03:52.445
Yeah.

63
00:03:52.447 --> 00:03:53.658
A few sessions ago.

64
00:03:53.660 --> 00:03:56.424
we talked about how you punish yourself.

65
00:03:56.426 --> 00:03:58.426
Do you think you deserve to be punished?

66
00:04:02.014 --> 00:04:03.094
I think I do.

67
00:04:04.267 --> 00:04:06.308
I feel like I've let my friends down

68
00:04:06.310 --> 00:04:08.601
and I'm not there for
them like I should be.

69
00:04:08.603 --> 00:04:11.271
I've been asking
around trying to find him.

70
00:04:11.273 --> 00:04:13.148
Pizza place doesn't know.

71
00:04:13.150 --> 00:04:16.066
So he meets up with Tyler
and then just disappears?

72
00:04:16.068 --> 00:04:18.296
He hasn't been in the neighborhood.

73
00:04:18.298 --> 00:04:20.571
I went and asked around the docks.

74
00:04:20.573 --> 00:04:22.739
I told you not to go down there.

75
00:04:22.741 --> 00:04:23.990
Oh.

76
00:04:23.992 --> 00:04:25.032
You "told me".

77
00:04:25.034 --> 00:04:28.202
You never did say what you were
doing there in the first place.

78
00:04:28.204 --> 00:04:32.038
Tony. my recovery is strong
enough to see some familiar faces.

79
00:04:32.040 --> 00:04:33.773
Forgive me if I'm not a big believer

80
00:04:33.775 --> 00:04:35.750
in people recovering at the moment.

81
00:04:37.004 --> 00:04:38.543
We don't know Tyler slipped.

82
00:04:39.505 --> 00:04:41.672
We don't know for sure what we even saw.

83
00:04:41.674 --> 00:04:44.550
Really? What did it look like to you?

84
00:04:44.552 --> 00:04:49.304
Yeah. but there's been nothing
since. right? Has he done anything?

85
00:04:49.306 --> 00:04:50.555
Said anything weird?

86
00:04:50.557 --> 00:04:51.806
He's Tyler.

87
00:04:51.808 --> 00:04:53.847
He says weird shit all the fucking time.

88
00:04:55.978 --> 00:04:58.874
Should we tell Alex about what we saw?

89
00:04:58.876 --> 00:05:00.608
You think we should tell Alex.

90
00:05:01.442 --> 00:05:02.861
Now I know you're worried.

91
00:05:06.446 --> 00:05:07.566
I believe in Tyler.

92
00:05:10.282 --> 00:05:11.865
I want to.

93
00:05:17.830 --> 00:05:20.750
I made a bunch of messes
I don't know how to clean up.

94
00:05:22.710 --> 00:05:23.710
Hey.

95
00:05:24.711 --> 00:05:25.721
Welcome back.

96
00:05:27.005 --> 00:05:28.045
Welcome back?

97
00:05:29.049 --> 00:05:30.049
Fuck you!

98
00:05:30.926 --> 00:05:32.056
Jesus.

99
00:05:33.219 --> 00:05:34.219
Zach. I...

100
00:05:35.679 --> 00:05:37.139
I don't know what happened.

101
00:05:38.057 --> 00:05:41.682
You mean after you crashed
my car and ditched me.

102
00:05:41.684 --> 00:05:44.002
I don't remember anything.
You gotta believe me.

103
00:05:44.004 --> 00:05:45.047
From before the party.

104
00:05:45.049 --> 00:05:46.979
Justin told me all kinds
of crazy shit happened.

105
00:05:46.981 --> 00:05:48.949
- and I don't remember.
- At some point.

106
00:05:48.951 --> 00:05:50.190
you had to have realized

107
00:05:50.192 --> 00:05:52.482
you crashed my car and
left me for dead. Right?

108
00:05:54.029 --> 00:05:56.318
I swear to God. I don't remember.

109
00:06:00.326 --> 00:06:01.326
Zach.

110
00:06:04.162 --> 00:06:05.752
You know. the crazy thing is...

111
00:06:08.208 --> 00:06:09.668
you didn't even seem scared.

112
00:06:10.710 --> 00:06:13.627
No. your eyes. it was like
you weren't even there.

113
00:06:13.629 --> 00:06:16.614
It was like you were... somebody else.

114
00:06:17.675 --> 00:06:19.877
Right before you drove
my car off the edge

115
00:06:19.879 --> 00:06:23.010
and sent me flying 30 fucking feet.

116
00:06:23.012 --> 00:06:25.179
Zach. I am so sorry.

117
00:06:25.181 --> 00:06:28.056
Don't worry about it. My
lawyer says he can get me off.

118
00:06:28.058 --> 00:06:31.810
He has a lot of practice. He
was Bryce's lawyer.

119
00:06:31.812 --> 00:06:33.603
It's funny. right?

120
00:06:33.605 --> 00:06:34.854
Um. no.

121
00:06:37.608 --> 00:06:38.608
Correct.

122
00:06:39.652 --> 00:06:42.652
None of this is fucking funny anymore.

123
00:06:42.654 --> 00:06:44.734
You are a goddamn
nightmare. so please...

124
00:06:46.491 --> 00:06:49.033
please just stay the
fuck out of my life.

125
00:06:49.035 --> 00:06:50.034
Forever.

126
00:06:55.749 --> 00:06:58.708
I've just... I've lost friends.

127
00:06:58.710 --> 00:07:00.501
I've made enemies.

128
00:07:00.503 --> 00:07:02.003
I need my life to change.

129
00:07:02.922 --> 00:07:05.213
something to. like. wake me up.

130
00:07:05.215 --> 00:07:08.465
He just sat there and
let the dummy bleed out.

131
00:07:09.428 --> 00:07:11.219
Luke. he saw the whole thing.

132
00:07:11.221 --> 00:07:12.887
Said it was fucking creepy.

133
00:07:12.889 --> 00:07:16.098
Oh. Well. maybe he didn't
like the sight of blood.

134
00:07:16.100 --> 00:07:18.785
It's kind of fucked up they're
making us learn that stuff.

135
00:07:18.787 --> 00:07:22.270
I'm just saying. He's this
close to full-blown psycho now.

136
00:07:22.272 --> 00:07:24.626
Well. that wouldn't have anything to do

137
00:07:24.628 --> 00:07:26.524
with you and your boys. would it?

138
00:07:26.526 --> 00:07:28.608
I told you. we're not
messing with him anymore.

139
00:07:28.610 --> 00:07:31.070
We got other ways to
figure out what he's hiding.

140
00:07:31.989 --> 00:07:33.830
What's that supposed to mean?

141
00:07:33.832 --> 00:07:35.659
Just that he's got a lot of friends...

142
00:07:36.451 --> 00:07:38.491
and one of them is
bound to know something.

143
00:07:39.996 --> 00:07:42.538
Well. you'd better
not do anything stupid.

144
00:07:42.540 --> 00:07:45.081
or you're just gonna get
yourself suspended again.

145
00:07:45.083 --> 00:07:47.042
Good thing I'm dating
the school president.

146
00:07:47.044 --> 00:07:49.664
Which means you really
don't want to piss me off.

147
00:07:50.922 --> 00:07:53.681
especially when we're
having so much fun together.

148
00:08:05.393 --> 00:08:07.013
Sit. Mr. Jensen.

149
00:08:08.729 --> 00:08:11.855
Not to be rude. but. like. who are you?

150
00:08:11.857 --> 00:08:12.981
Dean Foundry.

151
00:08:12.983 --> 00:08:15.941
Dean is your name or your title?

152
00:08:15.943 --> 00:08:18.573
Title. I'm the new
dean of discipline. Sit.

153
00:08:22.878 --> 00:08:23.948
Wait.

154
00:08:23.950 --> 00:08:25.784
Dean of which now?

155
00:08:25.786 --> 00:08:28.119
The district feels it
needs a more active role

156
00:08:28.121 --> 00:08:29.913
in monitoring the student body

157
00:08:29.915 --> 00:08:32.964
and managing disruptions to
the learning environment. and...

158
00:08:34.085 --> 00:08:36.835
it seems they're right. judging
from the smashed security cameras

159
00:08:36.837 --> 00:08:39.587
we've been dealing with
for the past two weeks.

160
00:08:39.589 --> 00:08:41.057
Can you account for your whereabouts

161
00:08:41.059 --> 00:08:43.767
between midnight and 7:00 a.m. today?

162
00:08:43.769 --> 00:08:46.228
- I'm guessing I was in bed.
- Guessing?

163
00:08:46.230 --> 00:08:47.397
I was in bed.

164
00:08:47.399 --> 00:08:50.193
- What time did you arrive at school?
- I don't know.

165
00:08:50.195 --> 00:08:51.905
- 9:30 or something.
- Or something?

166
00:08:53.684 --> 00:08:56.143
- 9:30.
- 9:47. actually.

167
00:08:56.145 --> 00:08:57.353
Almost two hours late.

168
00:08:57.355 --> 00:08:59.313
I was in an appointment.

169
00:08:59.315 --> 00:09:00.689
Right. ask my mom.

170
00:09:00.691 --> 00:09:02.357
I already have done.

171
00:09:02.359 --> 00:09:04.733
She wasn't aware of any appointment.

172
00:09:04.735 --> 00:09:06.609
She'll be speaking with you tonight.

173
00:09:07.489 --> 00:09:09.863
Anything you wanna tell
me about the cameras?

174
00:09:09.865 --> 00:09:12.074
Or who might have seen
fit to destroy them?

175
00:09:12.076 --> 00:09:13.951
No. Nothing I want to tell you.

176
00:09:13.953 --> 00:09:16.662
Well. if you think of anything
later. I'm always here.

177
00:09:17.747 --> 00:09:19.037
Now. back to class.

178
00:09:24.878 --> 00:09:25.928
Take good care.

179
00:09:29.216 --> 00:09:30.924
Wait. How...

180
00:09:30.926 --> 00:09:34.885
How did you know that I
got here at exactly 9:47?

181
00:09:34.887 --> 00:09:36.762
I know a lot. Clay.

182
00:09:36.764 --> 00:09:37.863
Get to class.

183
00:09:42.394 --> 00:09:43.893
Hey!

184
00:09:43.895 --> 00:09:45.645
Congrats on the interview.

185
00:09:46.982 --> 00:09:50.315
- Uh. what? What are you talking about?
- Brown.

186
00:09:50.317 --> 00:09:52.860
Uh. the alumni reps
are coming next week.

187
00:09:52.862 --> 00:09:55.528
I saw the schedule on Bolan's desk.

188
00:09:55.530 --> 00:09:57.447
That's gotta be a mistake. I...

189
00:09:57.449 --> 00:09:59.907
Not unless there's another
Clay Jensen around here

190
00:09:59.909 --> 00:10:02.452
I don't know about. which is. like...

191
00:10:02.454 --> 00:10:03.743
One is enough.

192
00:10:05.998 --> 00:10:07.539
But you...

193
00:10:07.541 --> 00:10:09.461
you did apply there. didn't you?

194
00:10:10.918 --> 00:10:11.958
I. uh...

195
00:10:12.753 --> 00:10:13.923
I mean. I guess.

196
00:10:31.687 --> 00:10:33.103
Hi.

197
00:10:33.105 --> 00:10:35.938
I didn't realize the door
under the stairs led anywhere.

198
00:10:35.940 --> 00:10:38.191
- Hi.
- It's quiet down here in the mornings.

199
00:10:38.193 --> 00:10:39.403
I get work done.

200
00:10:40.403 --> 00:10:42.861
I looked through my brother's
stuff like you asked.

201
00:10:42.863 --> 00:10:44.321
The police kept most of it.

202
00:10:44.323 --> 00:10:47.908
but I thought this might
be something to look at.

203
00:10:47.910 --> 00:10:50.451
- Schoolwork?
- A football playbook.

204
00:10:50.453 --> 00:10:53.245
I don't understand
the plays or anything.

205
00:10:53.247 --> 00:10:55.691
but while the coaches taught the plays.

206
00:10:55.693 --> 00:10:57.957
the guys wrote notes to each other.

207
00:10:57.959 --> 00:11:00.251
Monty. Bryce. Diego.

208
00:11:00.253 --> 00:11:05.592
There's. like. two years' worth.
from before and after Bryce died.

209
00:11:11.180 --> 00:11:14.679
Okay. "Es dudoso que...

210
00:11:16.017 --> 00:11:17.847
llover谩 ma帽ana".

211
00:11:19.354 --> 00:11:21.102
What?

212
00:11:21.104 --> 00:11:22.687
What?

213
00:11:22.689 --> 00:11:24.022
Nothing.

214
00:11:24.024 --> 00:11:27.692
See. you're using "que". so
it has to be the subjunctive.

215
00:11:27.694 --> 00:11:29.652
The subjunctive mood can also be used

216
00:11:29.654 --> 00:11:32.530
when expressing a speaker's
feelings about a perceived reality.

217
00:11:32.532 --> 00:11:34.073
"I'm sorry you're cold".

218
00:11:34.075 --> 00:11:36.194
Siento que tengas fr铆o.

219
00:11:37.702 --> 00:11:40.787
Tony. I'm sorry you have to hear
this. You could school us both.

220
00:11:40.789 --> 00:11:43.456
Yes. but it wouldn't be
nearly as entertaining.

221
00:11:45.042 --> 00:11:47.125
May I have your attention. please?

222
00:11:47.127 --> 00:11:50.337
We are currently moving
into a lockdown situation.

223
00:11:50.339 --> 00:11:51.587
Code Red.

224
00:11:51.589 --> 00:11:53.548
This is a hard lockdown.

225
00:11:53.550 --> 00:11:57.218
Staff. please initiate lockdown
procedures immediately.

226
00:11:57.220 --> 00:11:59.369
Students. please do not panic.

227
00:11:59.371 --> 00:12:01.221
and listen closely to this announcement

228
00:12:01.223 --> 00:12:03.181
and the instructions of your teacher.

229
00:12:03.183 --> 00:12:06.393
Seek immediate shelter
in the nearest classroom.

230
00:12:06.395 --> 00:12:09.436
I repeat. This is a Code
Red. Hard lockdown.

231
00:12:09.438 --> 00:12:11.711
Code Red. That's active shooter. right?

232
00:12:11.713 --> 00:12:13.774
Yeah. it's gotta be
another stupid drill.

233
00:12:13.776 --> 00:12:15.316
Okay. everyone listen up. please!

234
00:12:15.318 --> 00:12:17.267
I need some students to help
me barricade the doors.

235
00:12:17.269 --> 00:12:21.155
- You. you. You three. let's go.
- Come on. let's go. Come on.

236
00:12:21.157 --> 00:12:24.741
He. uh. doesn't look like
he was expecting a drill.

237
00:12:24.743 --> 00:12:27.243
- Let's get those lights off.
- What is it?

238
00:12:28.664 --> 00:12:29.746
Tyler's gone.

239
00:12:33.626 --> 00:12:35.597
The rest of you. stop what you're doing

240
00:12:35.599 --> 00:12:37.636
and you need to
shelter under the tables.

241
00:12:46.512 --> 00:12:48.178
Right here.

242
00:12:48.180 --> 00:12:49.388
Tony. hey.

243
00:12:49.390 --> 00:12:50.764
Hey. what is it?

244
00:12:50.766 --> 00:12:53.141
Yeah. what do you know?
What's up with Tyler?

245
00:12:53.143 --> 00:12:55.563
I think he's been buying guns.

246
00:13:01.191 --> 00:13:04.571
Okay. everybody. just
stay down. stay quiet.

247
00:13:27.798 --> 00:13:29.298
Come on. Quicker.

248
00:13:29.300 --> 00:13:31.760
Why can't we do this
bullshit when I have English?

249
00:13:36.473 --> 00:13:37.597
Hey. Justin.

250
00:13:37.599 --> 00:13:40.682
Once everyone's inside. lock
the doors. You know the protocol.

251
00:13:40.684 --> 00:13:43.685
All right. Coach. This
is just a drill. right?

252
00:13:43.687 --> 00:13:45.520
I'll see what I can find out.

253
00:13:45.522 --> 00:13:49.482
Hey. towards the back. in the
showers. Away from the doors.

254
00:13:49.484 --> 00:13:51.034
All right? Y'all stay low.

255
00:14:05.122 --> 00:14:06.122
Hey. man.

256
00:14:07.083 --> 00:14:08.133
You okay?

257
00:14:09.919 --> 00:14:12.088
Code Red means it's real. right?

258
00:14:13.713 --> 00:14:15.421
Hey. check it.

259
00:14:15.423 --> 00:14:17.924
No windows. Cement walls.

260
00:14:17.926 --> 00:14:21.095
And if someone does try and
come in here. we... we handle it.

261
00:14:22.096 --> 00:14:23.516
No one's getting hurt today.

262
00:14:25.349 --> 00:14:27.014
No talking.

263
00:14:29.769 --> 00:14:31.154
Why so concerned?

264
00:14:31.156 --> 00:14:34.278
Your boy Clay bring something
bigger than a knife this time?

265
00:14:34.280 --> 00:14:36.398
I've got a right to know.
I'm definitely on his list.

266
00:14:36.400 --> 00:14:39.484
- That's not even funny.
- No shit. it's not.

267
00:14:55.125 --> 00:14:56.290
For instance.

268
00:14:56.292 --> 00:14:59.081
I thought I helped my friend
Tyler after his assault.

269
00:14:59.878 --> 00:15:01.998
but now I'm not sure
I helped him enough.

270
00:15:19.813 --> 00:15:21.192
Or if I helped him at all.

271
00:15:26.694 --> 00:15:27.694
Oh. fuck.

272
00:15:33.575 --> 00:15:34.655
No!

273
00:15:57.763 --> 00:15:58.762
Fuck!

274
00:16:02.433 --> 00:16:05.223
Saw that one coming. didn't you?

275
00:16:07.228 --> 00:16:08.778
It's just a drill.

276
00:16:09.814 --> 00:16:11.606
- What if you're wrong?
- I'm not.

277
00:16:11.608 --> 00:16:13.858
- What if it's Tyler?
- It's not.

278
00:16:13.860 --> 00:16:15.275
Because what?

279
00:16:15.277 --> 00:16:16.447
He's better now?

280
00:16:18.447 --> 00:16:20.322
Because it's a drill.

281
00:16:20.324 --> 00:16:21.573
and. yes. he's better.

282
00:16:21.575 --> 00:16:23.824
What reason would he
have to do this again?

283
00:16:24.827 --> 00:16:26.197
Same reason as before.

284
00:16:27.205 --> 00:16:31.331
Me. everyone who treated him
like shit since he was seven.

285
00:16:31.333 --> 00:16:33.304
You of all people should know that.

286
00:16:33.306 --> 00:16:34.751
That shit doesn't just go away.

287
00:16:34.753 --> 00:16:38.337
It haunts you for the
rest of your fucking life...

288
00:16:38.339 --> 00:16:40.172
... which may end today.

289
00:16:40.174 --> 00:16:41.264
Fuck off.

290
00:16:49.766 --> 00:16:51.474
Are you scared?

291
00:16:51.476 --> 00:16:54.515
Are you feeling what terror actually is?

292
00:16:55.312 --> 00:16:57.687
The feeling of sitting here helpless.

293
00:16:57.689 --> 00:16:59.859
and death is on the
other side of that door.

294
00:17:01.108 --> 00:17:02.399
Yes.

295
00:17:02.401 --> 00:17:04.201
- Yes what?
- I'm scared!

296
00:17:10.450 --> 00:17:11.699
Yeah.

297
00:17:11.701 --> 00:17:12.911
I know that feeling.

298
00:17:29.092 --> 00:17:32.133
At the tone. please
record your voice message.

299
00:17:33.512 --> 00:17:35.679
Hey. Mom. it's me. Estela.

300
00:17:35.681 --> 00:17:39.598
I know you're at work.
but... just thought I'd call.

301
00:17:39.600 --> 00:17:42.730
They're doing one of those drills
again. I'm sure it's nothing.

302
00:17:44.063 --> 00:17:45.523
but you always said to call.

303
00:17:48.733 --> 00:17:50.323
I love you...

304
00:17:51.278 --> 00:17:52.898
so much.

305
00:18:10.210 --> 00:18:11.880
Come on.

306
00:18:22.805 --> 00:18:25.265
Jesus. Fuck!

307
00:18:27.517 --> 00:18:28.607
What are you doing?

308
00:18:29.728 --> 00:18:31.269
Code Red.

309
00:18:31.271 --> 00:18:33.937
Shooter. Did you not
hear the announcement?

310
00:18:33.939 --> 00:18:35.564
No.

311
00:18:35.566 --> 00:18:38.567
I was in the darkroom. I had these on.

312
00:18:38.569 --> 00:18:39.569
So...

313
00:18:42.739 --> 00:18:44.149
should we wait to die?

314
00:18:47.619 --> 00:18:49.159
Vicodin. huh?

315
00:18:49.161 --> 00:18:51.202
That's for the car accident?

316
00:18:51.204 --> 00:18:52.204
Uh-huh.

317
00:18:53.415 --> 00:18:55.206
And the vodka?

318
00:18:55.208 --> 00:18:56.458
That's just for fun?

319
00:18:57.418 --> 00:18:59.376
Sorry. I can smell it from here.

320
00:18:59.378 --> 00:19:01.926
Dude. you try walking
around with a broken arm

321
00:19:01.928 --> 00:19:03.547
and a fucked-up knee.

322
00:19:03.549 --> 00:19:06.633
If you keep judging me. I'm
lockin' you back up in your cave.

323
00:19:06.635 --> 00:19:07.635
No. I'm...

324
00:19:09.095 --> 00:19:10.145
not judging.

325
00:19:14.016 --> 00:19:16.726
But maybe you want to try something

326
00:19:17.895 --> 00:19:19.894
that might actually take the pain away.

327
00:19:22.565 --> 00:19:24.355
We're all. like. isolated.

328
00:19:25.276 --> 00:19:26.736
trying to make sense of it.

329
00:19:28.111 --> 00:19:29.411
Trying to hold on.

330
00:19:31.156 --> 00:19:32.616
Can I get my phone?

331
00:19:33.992 --> 00:19:37.034
Sorry. Rob. We need to stay low. okay?

332
00:19:38.412 --> 00:19:41.246
I just wanna text my
parents just to say goodbye.

333
00:19:41.248 --> 00:19:43.706
Hey. None of that.

334
00:19:43.708 --> 00:19:44.798
No goodbyes.

335
00:19:47.045 --> 00:19:48.045
Hey...

336
00:19:49.714 --> 00:19:51.843
don't they usually
tell you in advance...

337
00:19:52.925 --> 00:19:54.508
if it's a drill?

338
00:20:03.184 --> 00:20:04.350
All right. look.

339
00:20:04.352 --> 00:20:06.027
We're all gonna be fine.

340
00:20:06.029 --> 00:20:08.103
We just need to sit
tight till the all-clear.

341
00:20:08.105 --> 00:20:09.646
Or we nut up and bring the hurt

342
00:20:09.648 --> 00:20:12.065
instead of just waiting
around like sitting ducks!

343
00:20:12.067 --> 00:20:13.379
What the fuck are you gonna do?

344
00:20:13.381 --> 00:20:15.275
Swing at the bullets? Don't be stupid.

345
00:20:15.277 --> 00:20:16.568
At least I'm not a coward.

346
00:20:16.570 --> 00:20:18.696
- So you admit to being stupid?
- That's enough!

347
00:20:18.698 --> 00:20:21.000
Just set an example. Both of you.

348
00:20:21.002 --> 00:20:22.740
I take offense to being called stupid

349
00:20:22.742 --> 00:20:25.535
by a recovered addict who still
gets shit-faced at parties.

350
00:20:25.537 --> 00:20:26.869
You fuckin' kidding me?

351
00:20:26.871 --> 00:20:28.121
- Hey. Justin.
- Let's go.

352
00:20:28.123 --> 00:20:30.962
Listen. Justin. Let's go
check the doors in the office.

353
00:20:35.695 --> 00:20:37.572
Maybe we all have that moment of

354
00:20:37.574 --> 00:20:39.638
"what the hell have I done?"

355
00:20:39.640 --> 00:20:41.600
What do you think you're gonna find?

356
00:20:41.602 --> 00:20:42.842
Anything.

357
00:20:42.844 --> 00:20:45.301
Something to tell me
not to lose my shit.

358
00:20:45.303 --> 00:20:47.220
He doesn't want to hurt anyone.

359
00:20:47.222 --> 00:20:49.723
Not anymore. You guys know he's better.

360
00:20:49.725 --> 00:20:51.057
I'm not sure what I know.

361
00:20:51.059 --> 00:20:54.476
Charlie. you and me. we spend
more time with him than anyone.

362
00:20:54.478 --> 00:20:57.855
But didn't something change
after the cops called him in?

363
00:20:57.857 --> 00:20:59.107
What the fuck?

364
00:21:06.364 --> 00:21:09.948
Okay. there's gotta be an
explanation. It's not what we think.

365
00:21:09.950 --> 00:21:11.860
Or it's exactly what we think.

366
00:21:12.786 --> 00:21:15.955
We have to turn these
in and tell someone.

367
00:21:17.165 --> 00:21:19.415
Wait. hold on. We don't
know that this isn't a drill.

368
00:21:19.417 --> 00:21:21.042
Do you really wanna risk that?

369
00:21:21.044 --> 00:21:23.918
If it's real. what good will
it do to turn the photos in?

370
00:21:23.920 --> 00:21:25.670
- You think it'll stop this?
- It might!

371
00:21:25.672 --> 00:21:28.601
There's a chance. If there's a
chance. we gotta do something.

372
00:21:28.603 --> 00:21:31.467
We don't know that it's Tyler.
My dad said he was fine.

373
00:21:31.469 --> 00:21:33.452
Maybe your dad thinks
everything's fine for you.

374
00:21:33.454 --> 00:21:34.470
What does that mean?

375
00:21:34.472 --> 00:21:36.930
That I'm the one who
threw Tyler's guns away.

376
00:21:36.932 --> 00:21:39.373
and if I gave him a second chance.

377
00:21:39.375 --> 00:21:41.768
and he comes in. and he does this...

378
00:21:41.770 --> 00:21:43.687
All right. let's just take a second.

379
00:21:43.689 --> 00:21:46.022
and we can think about
what we need to do.

380
00:21:46.024 --> 00:21:48.115
If you're wrong about
this. his life is over.

381
00:21:48.117 --> 00:21:50.232
If he goes down. how long
do you think it's gonna be

382
00:21:50.234 --> 00:21:51.947
before we all go down too?

383
00:21:52.905 --> 00:21:55.237
Maybe we're all terrified to find out

384
00:21:55.239 --> 00:21:57.323
just what the hell have we done.

385
00:21:57.325 --> 00:21:58.908
Okay.

386
00:21:58.910 --> 00:22:02.209
Do we protect everyone
or just ourselves?

387
00:22:06.666 --> 00:22:07.666
It's a drill.

388
00:22:10.336 --> 00:22:12.242
Can't stop thinkin' about Tyler?

389
00:22:12.244 --> 00:22:14.213
Maybe it's not Tyler.

390
00:22:14.215 --> 00:22:15.506
Maybe it's another kid.

391
00:22:15.508 --> 00:22:18.466
There's. what. 1.000
kids at this school?

392
00:22:18.468 --> 00:22:20.843
You think Tyler's the first
to think about taking a gun

393
00:22:20.845 --> 00:22:24.555
and shooting as many kids as
he could before he died himself?

394
00:22:24.557 --> 00:22:26.807
Nah. I'm still Team Tyler.

395
00:22:26.809 --> 00:22:28.809
No. Tyler's better.

396
00:22:28.811 --> 00:22:30.769
You... you saw that.

397
00:22:30.771 --> 00:22:34.980
I did. but your plan's kinda
falling apart. isn't it?

398
00:22:36.317 --> 00:22:38.109
You don't know what Tyler's up to.

399
00:22:38.111 --> 00:22:41.027
I don't care. It's
not my problem anymore.

400
00:22:41.029 --> 00:22:42.654
It's not your problem?

401
00:22:42.656 --> 00:22:44.635
So you don't think if
someone out there put a gun

402
00:22:44.637 --> 00:22:47.492
to the head of. say. Jessica.

403
00:22:47.494 --> 00:22:49.284
you don't think she'd rat you out?

404
00:22:49.286 --> 00:22:50.994
Oh. or Alex? Or Zach?

405
00:22:50.996 --> 00:22:54.081
Or Justin. Jesus. I bet
he'd piss his little pants.

406
00:22:54.083 --> 00:22:55.874
No. he wouldn't. None of them would.

407
00:22:55.876 --> 00:22:59.043
Okay. what about you? What would
you do with a gun to your head?

408
00:22:59.045 --> 00:23:00.385
I've had a gun to my head.

409
00:23:01.172 --> 00:23:04.131
I've had an AR-15 here.

410
00:23:04.133 --> 00:23:08.218
Right here. and I survived.
and I did the right thing.

411
00:23:08.220 --> 00:23:11.096
'Cause you're Clay
Jensen. You're Liberty High's hero.

412
00:23:11.098 --> 00:23:13.347
You've stared down the
barrel once already.

413
00:23:13.349 --> 00:23:14.703
Hell. you drove off the road

414
00:23:14.705 --> 00:23:16.729
'cause you're not scared
of anything. right?

415
00:23:19.396 --> 00:23:21.020
Are you a hero

416
00:23:21.022 --> 00:23:22.730
or a martyr?

417
00:23:30.114 --> 00:23:33.282
It's just a teacher. checking the locks.

418
00:23:33.284 --> 00:23:34.284
Maybe.

419
00:23:41.791 --> 00:23:45.250
So you're not afraid to die.
just as. like. a general thing?

420
00:23:46.128 --> 00:23:48.295
Maybe I just don't care anymore.

421
00:23:48.297 --> 00:23:51.338
You say that. but
speaking from experience.

422
00:23:51.340 --> 00:23:53.893
you really do 'cause once you're gone.

423
00:23:53.895 --> 00:23:55.968
all that's left is the
shit you didn't do.

424
00:23:55.970 --> 00:23:59.679
Or the shit that you did
do. but you did wrong.

425
00:24:01.892 --> 00:24:04.017
I always tried to do the right thing.

426
00:24:04.019 --> 00:24:05.019
Did you?

427
00:24:06.353 --> 00:24:07.773
If you die today.

428
00:24:08.856 --> 00:24:11.023
is your conscience clear?

429
00:24:11.025 --> 00:24:12.900
I'm not dying today.

430
00:24:12.902 --> 00:24:15.401
No one can ever say that and know.

431
00:24:27.831 --> 00:24:28.872
Fuck.

432
00:25:34.180 --> 00:25:37.390
- Have you been in here the whole time?
- I'm sorry.

433
00:25:37.392 --> 00:25:39.264
I was gonna say something earlier.

434
00:25:39.266 --> 00:25:41.309
but then I heard you
talking on the phone.

435
00:25:41.311 --> 00:25:43.521
and I heard you say your name.

436
00:25:45.524 --> 00:25:47.323
Oh... right.

437
00:25:50.069 --> 00:25:53.445
I'm sorry we haven't
ever. like. officially met.

438
00:25:53.447 --> 00:25:55.953
I was gonna say something. sometime.

439
00:25:55.955 --> 00:25:58.116
but I just didn't know what to say.

440
00:25:58.118 --> 00:25:59.118
It's fine.

441
00:26:00.161 --> 00:26:01.161
I get it.

442
00:26:04.290 --> 00:26:05.540
It's just a drill.

443
00:26:06.333 --> 00:26:08.623
At least that's what I think it is.

444
00:26:09.378 --> 00:26:10.377
Yeah.

445
00:26:11.754 --> 00:26:12.794
It's just...

446
00:26:14.215 --> 00:26:17.674
... this is the last place
in the world I want to be.

447
00:26:22.431 --> 00:26:23.431
Oh...

448
00:26:30.563 --> 00:26:33.562
Everyone's past is the
reason for what they do today.

449
00:26:45.075 --> 00:26:46.450
Hi. Ani.

450
00:26:46.452 --> 00:26:47.662
Hey. it's me. Jess.

451
00:26:49.412 --> 00:26:53.422
Look. I'm sorry I haven't
texted you or called you at all.

452
00:26:54.709 --> 00:26:56.248
I hope your mom's doing okay.

453
00:26:58.837 --> 00:27:02.756
Listen. uh. the night that
you left. you said something.

454
00:27:02.758 --> 00:27:03.797
You said. um...

455
00:27:04.967 --> 00:27:07.797
hating weakness doesn't
make us stronger.

456
00:27:10.514 --> 00:27:12.923
I thought I knew what you meant. but...

457
00:27:15.435 --> 00:27:17.055
... now I don't know.

458
00:27:18.772 --> 00:27:20.321
I was just wondering...

459
00:27:22.358 --> 00:27:23.568
if you meant me?

460
00:27:28.738 --> 00:27:30.446
Sorry. Anyway...

461
00:27:30.448 --> 00:27:34.118
... you don't. um. need to
call me back. I'm being dumb.

462
00:27:35.285 --> 00:27:36.415
I'll talk to you.

463
00:27:40.457 --> 00:27:41.457
I miss you.

464
00:27:44.126 --> 00:27:45.796
Tell your mom I said get well.

465
00:27:49.465 --> 00:27:50.464
Bye.

466
00:27:55.887 --> 00:27:56.897
Dude...

467
00:27:58.931 --> 00:28:00.011
shit's weak.

468
00:28:00.808 --> 00:28:02.098
I don't feel anything.

469
00:28:03.644 --> 00:28:07.693
I expected quality premium
substances from you. Hillcrest boy.

470
00:28:08.940 --> 00:28:11.320
You have eaten

471
00:28:12.235 --> 00:28:14.234
all of the yearbook's snacks.

472
00:28:14.236 --> 00:28:16.736
That's the last of my lunch. so...

473
00:28:17.572 --> 00:28:19.072
... you're stoned.

474
00:28:19.074 --> 00:28:21.305
Mm-mm. You're talking to
the guy that's been fucked up

475
00:28:21.307 --> 00:28:22.866
for half a semester.

476
00:28:22.868 --> 00:28:24.288
I think I'd know if I was...

477
00:28:36.463 --> 00:28:39.253
So why are you always fucked up?

478
00:28:42.553 --> 00:28:44.342
It's fuckin' high school. man.

479
00:28:45.555 --> 00:28:47.805
People suck.

480
00:28:50.017 --> 00:28:51.357
Your friends suck.

481
00:28:53.270 --> 00:28:55.854
I learned that in Burnham Woods.

482
00:28:55.856 --> 00:28:57.986
You talkin' about what
happened with Alex?

483
00:28:59.192 --> 00:29:00.231
You know about it?

484
00:29:01.694 --> 00:29:02.694
Yeah.

485
00:29:03.779 --> 00:29:05.195
So. yeah.

486
00:29:05.197 --> 00:29:08.489
Come to me when your boyfriend
breaks up with you for no reason

487
00:29:08.491 --> 00:29:11.701
and won't even look at ya
and basically hates your guts.

488
00:29:11.703 --> 00:29:13.744
Don't pretend to be innocent. okay?

489
00:29:13.746 --> 00:29:14.796
You lied to him.

490
00:29:15.706 --> 00:29:17.302
How's anybody supposed to believe

491
00:29:17.304 --> 00:29:19.583
you actually gave a shit about Alex?

492
00:29:19.585 --> 00:29:22.960
I do give a shit about Alex.

493
00:29:22.962 --> 00:29:25.337
- I give lots of shits.
- Mm-hmm.

494
00:29:25.339 --> 00:29:27.299
I wasn't playing him.

495
00:29:28.176 --> 00:29:29.256
I loved him.

496
00:29:30.360 --> 00:29:31.650
I still do.

497
00:29:31.652 --> 00:29:32.731
Yeah?

498
00:29:32.733 --> 00:29:35.443
What did you love about him exactly?

499
00:29:37.058 --> 00:29:38.515
He's. like.

500
00:29:38.517 --> 00:29:40.517
the kindest person I've ever met.

501
00:29:45.691 --> 00:29:46.690
Yeah.

502
00:29:49.360 --> 00:29:50.360
Wait.

503
00:29:51.112 --> 00:29:52.778
Are you in love with him too?

504
00:29:52.780 --> 00:29:53.829
No.

505
00:29:57.451 --> 00:29:58.961
But I..

506
00:30:00.496 --> 00:30:01.535
I do love him.

507
00:30:02.705 --> 00:30:05.085
He's a good person. really.

508
00:30:06.542 --> 00:30:08.712
I've done a lot of
fucked-up shit. and...

509
00:30:10.462 --> 00:30:11.792
he never judges me.

510
00:30:14.966 --> 00:30:16.924
You've done some shit?

511
00:30:16.926 --> 00:30:18.425
Like what?

512
00:30:22.056 --> 00:30:23.396
Oh. shit.

513
00:30:24.641 --> 00:30:25.641
Fuck.

514
00:30:31.481 --> 00:30:32.900
Oh. shit. Did you see that?

515
00:30:36.610 --> 00:30:37.610
Fuck.

516
00:30:39.738 --> 00:30:41.817
This isn't a drill.

517
00:30:42.865 --> 00:30:45.533
And we try to clean
up the messes we've made.

518
00:30:45.535 --> 00:30:46.742
He's our friend. Tony.

519
00:30:46.744 --> 00:30:48.993
I know that. Of course I know that.

520
00:30:48.995 --> 00:30:52.121
We all want to protect Tyler
and believe that he's better.

521
00:30:52.123 --> 00:30:53.790
- What if we're wrong?
- Yeah.

522
00:30:55.293 --> 00:30:57.084
What was that?

523
00:30:57.086 --> 00:30:58.252
Oh. shit.

524
00:31:03.299 --> 00:31:06.175
Fuck this. I'm taking this
stuff to Foundry right now.

525
00:31:06.177 --> 00:31:08.137
What... ? No!

526
00:31:12.224 --> 00:31:14.182
Alex. are you okay?

527
00:31:14.184 --> 00:31:15.267
I did this.

528
00:31:15.269 --> 00:31:18.061
Everyone's gonna
die. and it's all my fault.

529
00:31:18.063 --> 00:31:19.687
What? No.

530
00:31:19.689 --> 00:31:22.189
Tony was right. Maybe
we coulda stopped him.

531
00:31:22.191 --> 00:31:23.232
I fu...

532
00:31:23.234 --> 00:31:25.943
I fucked this up like I fuck
up everything!

533
00:31:25.945 --> 00:31:28.114
Alex. hey. listen to me. Listen.

534
00:31:29.364 --> 00:31:32.282
I can't breathe.

535
00:31:32.284 --> 00:31:33.908
I think I'm dying.

536
00:31:33.910 --> 00:31:35.409
Huh? Uh...

537
00:31:36.161 --> 00:31:39.746
Focus on your hands. What do
you feel like? Describe it to me.

538
00:31:39.748 --> 00:31:41.582
I don't fucking know!

539
00:31:43.209 --> 00:31:45.334
Just squeeze my hands.

540
00:31:45.336 --> 00:31:46.961
Okay. you can do that.

541
00:31:46.963 --> 00:31:48.254
Come on. I know you can.

542
00:31:49.424 --> 00:31:52.591
Come on. Alex. Focus on me. Okay?

543
00:31:52.593 --> 00:31:54.467
- Just breathe.
- Okay.

544
00:31:54.469 --> 00:31:57.012
Breathe.

545
00:31:57.014 --> 00:31:58.183
You got it.

546
00:32:00.683 --> 00:32:01.733
It's gonna be okay.

547
00:32:03.352 --> 00:32:04.476
Just breathe.

548
00:32:10.275 --> 00:32:12.108
I think he's gone.

549
00:32:12.110 --> 00:32:14.693
Do you think he'll find us in here?

550
00:32:14.695 --> 00:32:16.278
I don't know.

551
00:32:16.280 --> 00:32:19.364
Sounds like he's moving
away. but if he comes back.

552
00:32:19.366 --> 00:32:21.616
bathroom doors can make great shields.

553
00:32:21.618 --> 00:32:25.077
They're two layers of
a really heavy metal.

554
00:32:25.079 --> 00:32:26.209
We're gonna be fine.

555
00:32:27.999 --> 00:32:30.378
Why would someone do
something like this?

556
00:32:32.085 --> 00:32:33.915
Maybe they're in a lot of pain.

557
00:32:35.922 --> 00:32:38.131
and they think that
this'll make it stop.

558
00:32:39.634 --> 00:32:42.304
Why would hurting
someone else make it stop?

559
00:32:43.137 --> 00:32:44.136
It doesn't.

560
00:32:45.221 --> 00:32:47.221
but you don't know that. You're just...

561
00:32:48.308 --> 00:32:49.858
You're so sad.

562
00:32:51.311 --> 00:32:53.390
and that sadness makes you angry...

563
00:32:54.146 --> 00:32:55.562
all the time.

564
00:32:55.564 --> 00:32:59.899
Like you thought
making a fist would feel good.

565
00:32:59.901 --> 00:33:00.983
and it does.

566
00:33:00.985 --> 00:33:02.568
You feel strong again.

567
00:33:02.570 --> 00:33:04.445
but then you can never...

568
00:33:04.447 --> 00:33:06.238
never unclench that fist.

569
00:33:06.240 --> 00:33:07.609
and you just feel like...

570
00:33:08.533 --> 00:33:10.783
like you just need to hurt someone else.

571
00:33:12.329 --> 00:33:14.449
Did you hurt someone else?

572
00:33:17.249 --> 00:33:18.419
I almost did.

573
00:33:20.378 --> 00:33:22.336
but my friends...

574
00:33:22.338 --> 00:33:23.707
helped me get better.

575
00:33:25.590 --> 00:33:27.630
I'm glad that you didn't do anything.

576
00:33:31.970 --> 00:33:32.970
Me too.

577
00:33:35.891 --> 00:33:38.400
I'm sorry for what
my brother did to you.

578
00:33:40.937 --> 00:33:43.107
everything that you had to go through.

579
00:33:44.732 --> 00:33:45.731
Thank you.

580
00:33:46.733 --> 00:33:49.523
I wonder if Monty could
have gotten better...

581
00:33:50.529 --> 00:33:51.909
if he had the chance.

582
00:33:53.447 --> 00:33:54.737
I guess. yeah.

583
00:33:55.533 --> 00:33:56.653
He fucked up.

584
00:33:59.036 --> 00:34:00.576
but I loved him.

585
00:34:02.706 --> 00:34:05.296
He was lucky to have you for a sister.

586
00:34:06.209 --> 00:34:08.719
It means he had something
good in his life.

587
00:34:16.385 --> 00:34:17.724
Mom. Hi.

588
00:34:20.555 --> 00:34:23.013
Oh. no. Nothing's wrong.

589
00:34:23.015 --> 00:34:24.091
I just. um...

590
00:34:24.093 --> 00:34:28.432
I was on my free period. and
I was just missing you guys.

591
00:34:30.605 --> 00:34:31.695
How's Seattle?

592
00:34:36.610 --> 00:34:38.070
Oh. that's so cool!

593
00:34:40.613 --> 00:34:42.373
I can't wait to visit you guys.

594
00:34:47.245 --> 00:34:48.864
How are Elijah and Cooper?

595
00:34:56.335 --> 00:34:58.755
Oh. my God. You're kidding me?

596
00:35:02.425 --> 00:35:06.004
Can you tell them I love
them... for me. please?

597
00:35:09.973 --> 00:35:10.972
Yeah.

598
00:35:23.735 --> 00:35:25.485
Hey. Mom. um...

599
00:35:25.487 --> 00:35:27.576
I actually have to go now.

600
00:35:31.408 --> 00:35:32.408
Yeah.

601
00:35:37.079 --> 00:35:38.079
I love you.

602
00:35:43.126 --> 00:35:44.466
Okay.

603
00:35:45.295 --> 00:35:46.295
Bye.

604
00:36:06.146 --> 00:36:09.439
Hey. what the hell do you think
you're doin'? Get back in there.

605
00:36:09.441 --> 00:36:12.150
Those were gunshots. We can't sit
here and let people get killed.

606
00:36:12.152 --> 00:36:14.902
Look. that hero talk
ain't worth your lives.

607
00:36:14.904 --> 00:36:16.904
I'm done hiding. and I don't run.

608
00:36:16.906 --> 00:36:20.573
No. see. you fight
as a last resort only.

609
00:36:20.575 --> 00:36:23.365
Now go sit the fuck down.

610
00:36:25.580 --> 00:36:27.090
All right. come on. Diego.

611
00:36:28.123 --> 00:36:29.873
People are scared.

612
00:36:29.875 --> 00:36:31.045
Well. I ain't scared.

613
00:36:32.086 --> 00:36:33.627
I'm ready to fight.

614
00:36:33.629 --> 00:36:34.629
Okay.

615
00:36:36.297 --> 00:36:38.117
Why aren't you. Foley?

616
00:36:38.119 --> 00:36:39.715
You don't want to stand and fight?

617
00:36:39.717 --> 00:36:42.260
You don't even know
where Jessica is. do you?

618
00:36:42.262 --> 00:36:44.681
You're okay to just let her die.

619
00:36:47.099 --> 00:36:48.223
Fuck!

620
00:36:48.225 --> 00:36:50.016
Hey. Okay. enough!

621
00:36:50.018 --> 00:36:52.726
Back in there!

622
00:36:52.728 --> 00:36:53.728
Let's go!

623
00:36:55.064 --> 00:36:57.774
Coach. come on. please! I
don't wanna die like this!

624
00:36:58.984 --> 00:37:00.521
If this is the last day of my life.

625
00:37:00.523 --> 00:37:02.402
I want to be doing the right thing.

626
00:37:02.404 --> 00:37:04.487
It's not gonna be the
last day of anyone's lives.

627
00:37:04.489 --> 00:37:06.114
No one's goin' anywhere. okay?

628
00:37:08.325 --> 00:37:10.745
Okay. everyone. Sit down!

629
00:37:13.247 --> 00:37:14.247
Head count.

630
00:37:18.501 --> 00:37:19.501
Coach...

631
00:37:21.212 --> 00:37:22.211
Foley.

632
00:37:33.014 --> 00:37:35.347
We try to unburden ourselves.

633
00:37:35.349 --> 00:37:38.188
I can't believe I survived
a roll-over crash for this.

634
00:37:40.103 --> 00:37:43.104
Death is playing games with
me. It's just a matter of time.

635
00:37:43.106 --> 00:37:45.645
And no offense. 'cause...

636
00:37:46.442 --> 00:37:48.942
you're actually cooler than I
thought you were gonna be. but...

637
00:37:51.655 --> 00:37:53.779
I don't wanna die with you.

638
00:37:53.781 --> 00:37:54.861
Don't worry.

639
00:37:56.075 --> 00:37:58.242
I don't wanna die with you either.

640
00:38:01.163 --> 00:38:03.413
Jesus.

641
00:38:05.000 --> 00:38:06.249
Jesus!

642
00:38:10.796 --> 00:38:13.176
Listen. if...

643
00:38:15.259 --> 00:38:18.088
if I die and you live...

644
00:38:24.600 --> 00:38:26.683
... will you tell him something for me?

645
00:38:26.685 --> 00:38:27.775
Alex?

646
00:38:29.396 --> 00:38:30.396
Yes.

647
00:38:31.315 --> 00:38:35.284
Will you tell him he's the
first boy I ever truly loved?

648
00:38:39.821 --> 00:38:42.364
Okay.

649
00:38:42.366 --> 00:38:43.406
Yeah. I'll do that.

650
00:38:51.874 --> 00:38:53.534
I beat up Bryce.

651
00:38:54.418 --> 00:38:55.959
What?

652
00:38:55.961 --> 00:38:57.091
The night he died.

653
00:38:58.088 --> 00:38:59.128
I beat him up.

654
00:39:02.008 --> 00:39:03.347
- You killed him?
- No.

655
00:39:04.551 --> 00:39:05.704
No. I went to the police.

656
00:39:05.706 --> 00:39:08.637
They told me that he didn't
die from getting beaten up.

657
00:39:08.639 --> 00:39:10.229
I still feel like shit. though.

658
00:39:11.432 --> 00:39:14.062
That maybe he wouldn't have
died if it wasn't for me.

659
00:39:18.814 --> 00:39:20.024
If I die.

660
00:39:22.359 --> 00:39:23.359
and you live.

661
00:39:24.736 --> 00:39:25.985
would you please...

662
00:39:29.407 --> 00:39:31.577
would you tell Miss
Walker that I'm sorry?

663
00:39:34.995 --> 00:39:35.995
Of course.

664
00:39:41.709 --> 00:39:42.709
Thanks. man.

665
00:39:52.427 --> 00:39:54.019
See? Now that would freak me out.

666
00:39:54.021 --> 00:39:56.021
That sounds like more than just a drill.

667
00:39:56.023 --> 00:39:57.220
Mm. a lot more.

668
00:39:57.222 --> 00:39:58.930
Shut up! Just... just...

669
00:39:58.932 --> 00:40:00.640
just shut up!

670
00:40:00.642 --> 00:40:03.059
Okay. Say it isn't Tyler.
Say it's another kid.

671
00:40:03.061 --> 00:40:05.628
Oh. like little Roddy Corman
who stood up at the assembly.

672
00:40:05.630 --> 00:40:08.190
I don't know why anyone would
want to fuck with that little shit.

673
00:40:08.958 --> 00:40:12.358
- Jesus. you're disgusting.
- Okay. Whatever. Sorry.

674
00:40:12.360 --> 00:40:14.569
It's that sweet. young Roddy.

675
00:40:14.571 --> 00:40:16.404
He just couldn't go on.

676
00:40:16.406 --> 00:40:19.449
Or it's another kid. gets beat at home.

677
00:40:19.451 --> 00:40:21.410
Tryin' to figure out his sexuality.

678
00:40:22.244 --> 00:40:23.364
Angry all the time.

679
00:40:24.121 --> 00:40:25.581
Why aren't you saving him?

680
00:40:26.957 --> 00:40:28.539
Tyler was my friend.

681
00:40:28.541 --> 00:40:30.961
So only your friends
deserve to be saved.

682
00:40:32.128 --> 00:40:35.383
Everyone deserves to be saved.

683
00:40:35.385 --> 00:40:37.172
Then why aren't you saving him?

684
00:40:37.174 --> 00:40:38.757
Then why didn't you save me?

685
00:40:38.759 --> 00:40:39.759
And me?

686
00:40:41.720 --> 00:40:45.304
Now. what happens when one
of those doors opens. Clay?

687
00:40:45.306 --> 00:40:47.848
Some sub didn't know you
need to pull on the door.

688
00:40:47.850 --> 00:40:50.017
so the deadbolt goes
into the strike plate.

689
00:40:50.019 --> 00:40:51.851
Didn't get locked all the way.

690
00:40:51.853 --> 00:40:54.361
Kid gets the door open.
and he sees 20 sophomores

691
00:40:54.363 --> 00:40:56.113
huddled under two tables.

692
00:40:56.941 --> 00:40:58.111
There's nowhere to run.

693
00:40:59.026 --> 00:41:00.400
Sitting ducks.

694
00:41:00.402 --> 00:41:01.735
Fish in a barrel.

695
00:41:01.737 --> 00:41:04.154
You know. he's got a 60-round
magazine and a bump stock.

696
00:41:04.156 --> 00:41:05.989
and they're gone in a minute.

697
00:41:05.991 --> 00:41:09.580
Femoral bleed. hearts burst
by bullets. skulls shattered.

698
00:41:11.037 --> 00:41:14.662
Shut the fuck up! Leave me alone!
Just leave me the fuck alone!

699
00:41:16.500 --> 00:41:18.040
Fuck!

700
00:41:24.965 --> 00:41:27.715
So now 23 kids and a teacher are dead.

701
00:41:28.511 --> 00:41:30.267
She died trying to shield them.

702
00:41:30.269 --> 00:41:31.850
The bullets went right through her.

703
00:41:34.974 --> 00:41:36.054
Clay. that kid.

704
00:41:37.185 --> 00:41:39.014
the kid that you couldn't save.

705
00:41:40.521 --> 00:41:42.395
what happens to him now?

706
00:41:42.397 --> 00:41:46.273
Does he still deserve
to be saved. or should he die?

707
00:41:46.275 --> 00:41:48.192
No one should die.

708
00:41:48.194 --> 00:41:50.820
Before he got to those sophomores
under the table in the room

709
00:41:50.822 --> 00:41:54.239
with the broken door.
before he got there.

710
00:41:54.241 --> 00:41:56.199
- he shot Tony.
- No!

711
00:41:56.201 --> 00:41:58.284
He shot Alex...

712
00:41:58.286 --> 00:41:59.586
he shot Justin.

713
00:42:01.038 --> 00:42:02.368
and you couldn't stop it.

714
00:42:03.582 --> 00:42:05.042
You couldn't save anyone.

715
00:42:07.920 --> 00:42:09.629
I...

716
00:42:12.173 --> 00:42:14.723
I can't save anyone.

717
00:42:18.929 --> 00:42:20.299
I never could.

718
00:42:23.225 --> 00:42:26.600
- And you found this in Tyler Down's bag?
- Yes. sir.

719
00:42:26.602 --> 00:42:30.192
I thought. what if this is him. right?

720
00:42:31.439 --> 00:42:32.649
No. it's good thinking.

721
00:42:33.441 --> 00:42:36.741
No. it's good you brought it to
me. I'll certainly look into this.

722
00:42:38.279 --> 00:42:41.530
Are you going to do something.
like. now. like something?

723
00:42:41.532 --> 00:42:42.781
- Call someone?
- Hush.

724
00:42:42.783 --> 00:42:45.367
I think it's best we handle
it after the lockdown.

725
00:42:45.369 --> 00:42:47.827
But what if there's something
you can do now. and...

726
00:42:47.829 --> 00:42:49.829
There's nothing to be done right now.

727
00:42:49.831 --> 00:42:52.623
- We'll handle it.
- How?

728
00:42:52.625 --> 00:42:54.125
- We'll handle it.
- Fuck.

729
00:42:54.127 --> 00:42:57.043
Thank you. Mr. Padilla. No. stay here.

730
00:42:57.045 --> 00:42:58.920
Gonna wait for the all-clear.

731
00:43:02.967 --> 00:43:04.005
Shit!

732
00:43:04.007 --> 00:43:05.007
Fuck.

733
00:43:06.012 --> 00:43:07.012
Fuck.

734
00:43:16.605 --> 00:43:17.735
Oh. shit. okay.

735
00:43:18.564 --> 00:43:19.564
Fuck.

736
00:43:26.988 --> 00:43:29.113
Hey. hold on! No gun!

737
00:43:29.115 --> 00:43:30.455
Aah!

738
00:43:32.035 --> 00:43:34.164
What the fuck?

739
00:43:36.705 --> 00:43:37.705
Hey.

740
00:43:38.874 --> 00:43:41.543
But sometimes the weight
of what we carry is too much.

741
00:43:42.460 --> 00:43:43.751
That's my dad.

742
00:43:43.753 --> 00:43:44.753
What?

743
00:43:45.713 --> 00:43:48.172
My dad. He's out in the hallway.

744
00:43:48.174 --> 00:43:51.257
I don't... I don't
think anyone's out there.

745
00:43:51.259 --> 00:43:53.218
No. I hear him.

746
00:43:53.220 --> 00:43:54.761
- Alex. Stay down.
- Fuck. I hear him.

747
00:43:54.763 --> 00:43:58.430
No. that's my dad! He's right
out there. Can't you hear him?

748
00:43:58.432 --> 00:43:59.556
He needs to shut up.

749
00:43:59.558 --> 00:44:02.017
- No. it's my dad.
- You two. down. now.

750
00:44:02.019 --> 00:44:03.852
He's calling my name. He's out there.

751
00:44:03.854 --> 00:44:06.020
- Get down.
- I can hear him!

752
00:44:06.022 --> 00:44:08.731
- Tell him to get down.
- Shit. Uh...

753
00:44:08.733 --> 00:44:11.067
Alex. it's the TBI. Okay?
You're not hearing your dad.

754
00:44:11.069 --> 00:44:13.026
It's your brain making
you think you are.

755
00:44:13.028 --> 00:44:15.779
- He's not there. It's the stress.
- No. I hear him.

756
00:44:15.781 --> 00:44:19.281
Alex. it's not him. okay?
It's your mind. Trust me.

757
00:44:22.602 --> 00:44:23.661
Oh.

758
00:44:23.663 --> 00:44:26.333
Come on. Come on. Let's go.

759
00:44:29.209 --> 00:44:31.329
Sometimes it's too much to handle.

760
00:44:32.295 --> 00:44:33.505
What do we do then?

761
00:44:34.381 --> 00:44:36.670
So you still don't care
about anything. Clay?

762
00:44:38.008 --> 00:44:39.878
You still don't have any regrets?

763
00:44:41.095 --> 00:44:43.678
You're glad that I'm dead.
and he got blamed.

764
00:44:43.680 --> 00:44:47.014
- Leave me alone.
- Last day of your life.

765
00:44:47.016 --> 00:44:48.276
No need to keep secrets.

766
00:44:49.352 --> 00:44:50.891
Are you sorry?

767
00:44:52.229 --> 00:44:54.019
Are you sorry for what you did?

768
00:44:56.066 --> 00:44:57.106
Yes.

769
00:45:00.278 --> 00:45:01.948
Yes. I'm sorry.

770
00:45:03.364 --> 00:45:06.656
- Wow.
- I didn't think he'd actually admit it.

771
00:45:06.658 --> 00:45:08.324
We got through to him.

772
00:45:08.326 --> 00:45:11.494
It's too bad you won't live.
but then again. who does?

773
00:45:11.496 --> 00:45:13.579
Blade Runner. Nice.

774
00:45:13.581 --> 00:45:15.460
Well. we only know it 'cause he does.

775
00:45:25.591 --> 00:45:26.971
Am I going crazy?

776
00:45:30.262 --> 00:45:32.304
Asked and answered. no?

777
00:45:32.306 --> 00:45:34.139
Going crazy?

778
00:45:34.141 --> 00:45:36.011
My boy. you done gone.

779
00:45:44.675 --> 00:45:46.404
If there's someone
that needs to be saved.

780
00:45:46.406 --> 00:45:48.651
I'm gonna try to save them.

781
00:45:48.653 --> 00:45:50.363
And if this is the day that I die.

782
00:45:51.531 --> 00:45:52.900
then I die standing up.

783
00:45:56.243 --> 00:45:58.076
Though I still think
it's a fucking drill.

784
00:46:06.210 --> 00:46:08.169
My dad gave me this quote once.

785
00:46:09.129 --> 00:46:10.799
"If you're going through hell.

786
00:46:12.382 --> 00:46:13.548
keep going".

787
00:46:46.079 --> 00:46:47.458
No. no. no! Don't shoot!

788
00:46:50.332 --> 00:46:51.372
Um...

789
00:46:57.505 --> 00:46:59.046
Look. this...

790
00:46:59.048 --> 00:47:00.808
this doesn't have to go this way.

791
00:47:01.884 --> 00:47:04.133
Whatever you've done...

792
00:47:04.135 --> 00:47:05.345
... it can be okay.

793
00:47:06.137 --> 00:47:07.227
Okay? Just...

794
00:47:10.516 --> 00:47:11.766
please don't shoot.

795
00:47:12.726 --> 00:47:14.726
Don't shoot. Please.

796
00:47:26.780 --> 00:47:27.780
I...

797
00:47:33.494 --> 00:47:35.452
Clay! Clay Jensen!

798
00:47:35.454 --> 00:47:38.247
What the hell are you doing?

799
00:47:39.333 --> 00:47:42.458
Clay!

800
00:47:42.460 --> 00:47:43.960
Get in here! Get in here.

801
00:47:50.717 --> 00:47:51.797
Get down.

802
00:47:55.675 --> 00:47:56.882
Is this a drill?

803
00:47:56.884 --> 00:47:59.223
- What were you doin' in that hallway?
- Is this a drill?

804
00:47:59.225 --> 00:48:00.599
- Did you hear the gunshots?
- Yes!

805
00:48:00.601 --> 00:48:01.684
You did.

806
00:48:01.686 --> 00:48:05.061
- So. why did you leave your classroom?
- I thought it was a drill!

807
00:48:05.063 --> 00:48:06.604
Goddamn it. Clay.

808
00:48:06.606 --> 00:48:07.897
This is a hard lockdown.

809
00:48:07.899 --> 00:48:10.150
There were first responders
on the scene with guns drawn.

810
00:48:10.152 --> 00:48:12.526
You thought that was a drill?

811
00:48:12.528 --> 00:48:15.112
Another rule that just
didn't apply to you.

812
00:48:15.114 --> 00:48:17.364
so you thought you'd run
around and be a pain in my ass?

813
00:48:17.366 --> 00:48:19.144
No! Someone kept trying the door.

814
00:48:19.146 --> 00:48:20.283
and I thought someone might need help.

815
00:48:20.285 --> 00:48:22.743
and I didn't want to die sitting down!

816
00:48:27.958 --> 00:48:28.958
Yeah.

817
00:48:30.794 --> 00:48:33.174
- Wait.
- All right. Now listen to me.

818
00:48:34.214 --> 00:48:35.843
No. Look. It's okay.

819
00:48:36.757 --> 00:48:38.337
Clay. you are not gonna die.

820
00:48:39.677 --> 00:48:40.887
You are not gonna die.

821
00:48:41.929 --> 00:48:43.344
The bullets were blanks.

822
00:48:43.346 --> 00:48:44.929
The officers tried the doors.

823
00:48:44.931 --> 00:48:46.411
The alarms were to make sure

824
00:48:46.413 --> 00:48:49.225
that students and
teachers followed protocol.

825
00:48:49.227 --> 00:48:51.310
and the only one who didn't was you.

826
00:48:51.312 --> 00:48:55.022
- They... they pounded at the doors.
- Those were their instructions.

827
00:48:55.024 --> 00:48:56.398
The bullets were blanks?

828
00:48:56.400 --> 00:48:57.991
Simulated gunfire

829
00:48:57.993 --> 00:49:00.229
to make sure the students
will be able to recognize it.

830
00:49:02.489 --> 00:49:03.821
So it was a drill.

831
00:49:03.823 --> 00:49:05.163
Well. if it wasn't.

832
00:49:07.701 --> 00:49:08.791
you'd be dead.

833
00:49:19.170 --> 00:49:20.170
Wait here.

834
00:49:26.885 --> 00:49:28.715
Well. I'm going through hell.

835
00:49:30.930 --> 00:49:33.430
A lot of us are going through hell.

836
00:49:33.432 --> 00:49:34.432
Jess.

837
00:49:35.351 --> 00:49:37.180
that was a fuckin' stapler.

838
00:49:38.102 --> 00:49:40.102
If I had a gun. I would have shot you.

839
00:49:45.275 --> 00:49:47.115
You want to shoot me. don't you?

840
00:49:50.113 --> 00:49:51.988
Deep down. you always have.

841
00:49:51.990 --> 00:49:53.069
Oh. my God.

842
00:49:54.075 --> 00:49:57.995
Justin. you came out of
a window during alockdown.

843
00:49:58.829 --> 00:49:59.998
Who does that?

844
00:50:00.914 --> 00:50:02.622
I...

845
00:50:02.624 --> 00:50:03.624
I was...

846
00:50:06.044 --> 00:50:08.502
We were hiding in the locker room.

847
00:50:08.504 --> 00:50:10.214
and I was just thinking.

848
00:50:11.715 --> 00:50:14.465
what if this is the last
day of our life. you know?

849
00:50:16.135 --> 00:50:17.425
And then I realized...

850
00:50:18.221 --> 00:50:20.851
if this is the last day of my life.

851
00:50:22.100 --> 00:50:23.599
I want to spend it with you.

852
00:50:30.357 --> 00:50:31.356
Okay. uh...

853
00:50:34.026 --> 00:50:35.106
I guess I'll just...

854
00:50:36.988 --> 00:50:38.653
I'll just go back. okay?

855
00:50:38.655 --> 00:50:40.575
Oh. my God. shut the fuck up.

856
00:50:48.581 --> 00:50:51.206
This lockdown is all clear.

857
00:50:51.208 --> 00:50:54.584
I repeat. This lockdown is all clear.

858
00:50:54.586 --> 00:50:56.272
An announcement will be made shortly

859
00:50:56.274 --> 00:50:58.212
to provide staff and students...

860
00:51:01.384 --> 00:51:02.593
Tyler. it's over.

861
00:51:08.515 --> 00:51:09.514
Tyler?

862
00:51:16.230 --> 00:51:21.649
Yeah. that happened to me
before. last year early on. but...

863
00:51:21.651 --> 00:51:23.443
it hadn't happened in a while.

864
00:51:23.445 --> 00:51:24.985
That was the stress.

865
00:51:24.987 --> 00:51:27.946
Yeah. how did you know.
like. what it was?

866
00:51:27.948 --> 00:51:29.781
Uh. I. um..

867
00:51:29.783 --> 00:51:32.409
I googled TBIs a while back.

868
00:51:32.411 --> 00:51:36.537
just to. you know. uh...
know what they entailed.

869
00:51:36.539 --> 00:51:39.669
Like. what you were going through.

870
00:51:40.834 --> 00:51:42.164
Oh. yeah. Um...

871
00:51:43.503 --> 00:51:45.413
Yeah. you know. I'm a freak. so...

872
00:51:46.423 --> 00:51:47.423
No.

873
00:51:48.299 --> 00:51:49.381
No. no. no.

874
00:52:01.019 --> 00:52:03.109
That... was surprising.

875
00:52:04.396 --> 00:52:07.526
Surprising good or surprising bad?

876
00:52:13.446 --> 00:52:15.321
Well. you two recovered.

877
00:52:15.323 --> 00:52:16.697
Kind of.

878
00:52:18.451 --> 00:52:22.077
- What?
- Well. I shoulda seen that comin'.

879
00:52:22.079 --> 00:52:23.739
Wait. what did Foundry say?

880
00:52:24.915 --> 00:52:27.584
He. uh. said he was gonna look into it.

881
00:52:28.584 --> 00:52:30.381
and then he said he
heard from the office

882
00:52:30.383 --> 00:52:32.544
that this was just a fucking drill.

883
00:52:32.546 --> 00:52:36.925
Okay. so if the cops bring him in again.

884
00:52:38.510 --> 00:52:40.176
what is that gonna mean for us?

885
00:52:49.478 --> 00:52:50.727
Hey. listen.

886
00:52:51.646 --> 00:52:54.897
What I said earlier. about
what happened with Bryce.

887
00:52:54.899 --> 00:52:57.399
I was super out of it.

888
00:52:58.318 --> 00:53:01.831
And even though you
didn't kill Bryce that night.

889
00:53:01.833 --> 00:53:03.246
you don't want to be known as the guy

890
00:53:03.248 --> 00:53:05.483
who beat the shit out of
him before he died. right?

891
00:53:06.283 --> 00:53:07.283
Yeah.

892
00:53:08.244 --> 00:53:09.244
Exactly.

893
00:53:10.079 --> 00:53:11.079
Don't worry.

894
00:53:12.748 --> 00:53:13.997
I can keep a secret.

895
00:53:15.875 --> 00:53:16.875
Thanks. man.

896
00:53:17.669 --> 00:53:18.669
Sure.

897
00:53:20.755 --> 00:53:23.505
Except. here's the thing.

898
00:53:24.758 --> 00:53:27.342
If you know for a fact
you didn't kill Bryce.

899
00:53:27.344 --> 00:53:30.723
then you must know who did. right?

900
00:53:34.559 --> 00:53:36.058
- Fantastic job.
- Thanks.

901
00:53:36.060 --> 00:53:38.226
- Thank you very much.
- Thank you. sir.

902
00:53:38.228 --> 00:53:41.646
Gentlemen. thank you for
your expertise. for your training.

903
00:53:41.648 --> 00:53:43.940
A lot of us are going through hell...

904
00:53:43.942 --> 00:53:45.524
I understand this is not easy...

905
00:53:45.526 --> 00:53:47.175
... and I don't know how we keep going.

906
00:53:47.177 --> 00:53:48.610
You made a big difference today.

907
00:53:48.612 --> 00:53:49.822
What the fuck?

908
00:53:51.115 --> 00:53:55.116
What the actual fuck are you thinking?

909
00:53:55.118 --> 00:53:58.635
Clay. would you take a
seat in my office. please?

910
00:53:58.637 --> 00:54:02.122
No! I will not take
a seat in your office!

911
00:54:02.124 --> 00:54:05.584
You think that this is
the way to make us safe?

912
00:54:05.586 --> 00:54:07.793
You know what would make me feel safe?

913
00:54:07.795 --> 00:54:10.337
Not having to go to a
school with metal detectors

914
00:54:10.339 --> 00:54:13.340
or video cameras or
armed fucking guards!

915
00:54:13.342 --> 00:54:16.176
There's still class. folks.

916
00:54:16.178 --> 00:54:17.635
Okay? Bell has not rung.

917
00:54:17.637 --> 00:54:19.512
No. you're killing us!

918
00:54:19.514 --> 00:54:22.140
You are killing us! Don't you get that?

919
00:54:22.142 --> 00:54:23.891
You made a drill with gunshots

920
00:54:23.893 --> 00:54:26.571
and hammered down the door
to prepare us for what exactly?

921
00:54:26.573 --> 00:54:28.145
What it feels like to be hunted?

922
00:54:28.147 --> 00:54:29.791
To practice getting ready to die.

923
00:54:29.793 --> 00:54:32.356
to make us feel afraid for our lives?

924
00:54:32.358 --> 00:54:35.359
We already know how that feels!
You're scaring us to death!

925
00:54:35.361 --> 00:54:38.528
- Every day! Every day! Every day!
- Calm down. son.

926
00:54:38.530 --> 00:54:40.197
I am not your goddamn son!

927
00:54:40.199 --> 00:54:41.990
Get the fuck away from me!

928
00:54:43.076 --> 00:54:44.951
We are children!

929
00:54:44.953 --> 00:54:47.536
We're kids! We should be
living our fucking lives

930
00:54:47.538 --> 00:54:50.498
instead of practicing how to cheat
death. because you know what?

931
00:54:50.500 --> 00:54:52.625
Everybody fucking dies!

932
00:54:52.627 --> 00:54:54.626
Everybody dies!

933
00:54:54.628 --> 00:54:57.045
So. please. please let us live!

934
00:54:57.047 --> 00:54:58.463
We are trying to keep you alive.

935
00:54:58.465 --> 00:55:00.673
That's what every minute of
this drill has been about.

936
00:55:00.675 --> 00:55:04.718
No! It was about you checking
a fucking box. a regulation.

937
00:55:04.720 --> 00:55:07.805
a law. whatever the fuck.
because you know what?

938
00:55:07.807 --> 00:55:11.307
- You know what? We're not safe.
- That's enough.

939
00:55:11.309 --> 00:55:13.768
Hey. fuck you. "that's
enough". Who are you?

940
00:55:13.770 --> 00:55:15.686
Who are you to say it's enough?

941
00:55:15.688 --> 00:55:17.229
Who are you?

942
00:55:18.440 --> 00:55:19.940
Clay! Stop!

943
00:55:19.942 --> 00:55:21.483
- Clay!
- Am I safer now?

944
00:55:21.485 --> 00:55:24.693
Huh? I've got your gun! I've
got your gun! Am I safer?

945
00:55:24.695 --> 00:55:26.111
- Please.
- Look at me. I'm armed.

946
00:55:26.113 --> 00:55:27.441
Should I give this to a teacher

947
00:55:27.443 --> 00:55:29.740
so they can save their fucking class?

948
00:55:29.742 --> 00:55:31.332
Clay. please.

949
00:55:32.203 --> 00:55:33.506
Put the gun down.

950
00:55:33.508 --> 00:55:36.412
We'll go to my office.
and we will talk this over. okay?

951
00:55:36.414 --> 00:55:37.914
Come on.

952
00:55:42.878 --> 00:55:43.878
Tyler...

953
00:55:44.713 --> 00:55:46.333
what happened to us?

954
00:55:48.449 --> 00:55:49.529
What did you do?

955
00:55:53.179 --> 00:55:55.263
What did you do?

956
00:55:55.265 --> 00:55:56.764
I didn't do anything.

957
00:56:00.644 --> 00:56:03.644
Okay. Okay.

958
00:56:03.646 --> 00:56:05.604
- No!
- Hey!

959
00:56:05.606 --> 00:56:08.440
Get off me! Get off of me now!

960
00:56:08.442 --> 00:56:09.650
No!

961
00:56:09.652 --> 00:56:10.750
No. please!

962
00:56:10.752 --> 00:56:12.527
No! God. no!

963
00:56:12.529 --> 00:56:13.653
- No!
- No...

964
00:59:28.908 --> 00:59:30.908
Well done. Ed. Well done.

